      "correspondence": "The compact type is built by shifting integral entries into the nonnegative dominant range and twisting both blocks by the full determinant. The mixed-signature existence theorem applies the square-integrable kernel realization. The distant-scale argument chooses a model before passing it to the occurrence statement.",
